title: "Architecting a Regime-Aware Deep Reinforcement Learning Microservice Ecosystem for Explainable Algorithmic Trading"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gohil
    given-names: Devangsinh
    affiliation: "ECE Paris"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Devangsinh84/AI_Trading_Platform"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-10-18
abstract: >-
  MSc thesis project: a decoupled Python / .NET / React microservice architecture for
  explainable, regime-aware deep reinforcement learning trading, with a corrected evaluation
  pipeline (real returns, transaction costs, Sharpe ratio, maximum drawdown) and SHAP
  explanations of a PPO agent on S&P 500 and VIX data.
keywords:
  - deep reinforcement learning
  - algorithmic trading
  - explainable AI
  - SHAP
  - market regimes
  - microservices
